{
  // audit-ci configuration.
  //
  // Keep the allowlist empty unless an advisory truly has no upstream fix.
  // Each entry needs a dated justification naming why the advisory is not
  // reachable in the deployed application and what would make it reachable.
  //
  // GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9 (vitest <4.1.11, moderate): path traversal via @vitest/mocker
  //   redirect mock. vitest is dev-only and never ships to Vercel; exploiting it
  //   requires running a malicious test file locally or in CI. Upgrading to
  //   vitest 4.1.11+ caused shard-isolation regressions in Radix/UI component
  //   tests; revisit when that upgrade can be validated across the full suite.
  //
  // GHSA-qxg6-89mg-rqv8 (@vitest/mocker <4.1.12, moderate), added 2026-10-29:
  //   code injection via unauthenticated manual mock registration on the vitest
  //   dev server. Same dev-only reach as GHSA-82fw: vitest never ships to Vercel,
  //   and CI runs vitest without exposing its server. The only fix is vitest
  //   4.1.12+ (major bump from 3.2.7). Both vitest entries are due for removal
  //   by 2026-11-30 via that upgrade in its own PR.
  //
  // GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm (braces) removed 2026-10-29: npm audit no longer reports it.
  "high": true,
  "allowlist": ["GHSA-82fw-gwwq-j7x9", "GHSA-qxg6-89mg-rqv8"]
